 "license": "Not recorded. The source .blend carries no licence text and none was supplied with it. Fill this in before these assets are distributed outside the project. assets/farm/ATTRIBUTION.md carries the same warning beside the meshes.",
 "note": "Nine animals, one per GLB, each a single skinned mesh on its own armature with one clip called `Walk`. Sizes are the metres the GLBs actually occupy at rest -- the source is authored in metres, so preferredScale is naturalSize.y and an instance is placed at scale 1.0.\n\n  Two things a recipe author should know before scattering these. First, a scattered instance is *static*: world::scatter merges an asset's primitives into one mesh per material and the merge does not carry skin influences, so a farm animal in a scatter layer draws in its bind pose, identically, forever. That is fine for a herd on a far hillside and wrong for anything the camera looks at. An animal that has to move must arrive as a `gltf` node with an `animation` state -- by hand in a scene file, or as a hero, which is a real Gltf node and does copy the rig. Second, `variation.lean` is 0 on every entry and should stay there: a bush may lean, but an animal standing on four legs that leans is an animal falling over.\n\n  preferredDensity is deliberately tiny. These are punctuation in a landscape, not groundcover: the densest entry here is the chicken at one per 300 square metres, and the horse is one per five thousand.",
